Michiel Helvensteijn <nomail@please.com> writes:

(several juicy monsters on a bigroom level)

> And I want to eat several corpses if possible. You can't do that if there
> are still enemies around. But if they come to me first, I suppose I can
> grab their corpse and take it upstairs with me.

Many of the interesting corpses are quite heavy and may make you stressed
or worse, in which case you won't be able to get it up the stairs.
You probably won't get to eat all corpses you listed. It is quite possible
that you can eat only one of them.

I would start by killing the monsters you don't especially plan to eat.
Then choose which is the one you most want, and leave it as the last
hostile monster alive on the level, so the others won't interrupt you.
In between, try with the other interesting corpses if you can carry them
without being stressed. Otherwise, take a bite whenever you can, until the
corpse is either eaten or rotten away, but WATCH OUT FOR YOUR HP WHILE
DOING IT! 
And if (when) you get satiated and don't have an unfinished corpse you
still want to eat, retreat to the previous level until you are no longer
satiated.

